---
/**
 * Home page. Every word of prose below is Kyle's, governed by §6 of the
 * handoff — do not reword, tighten or "improve" any of it. The corrections
 * listed there were each made deliberately and several were reverted once
 * already after a draft undid them.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../data/portrait.txt?raw';
import projects from '../data/projects.json';

const title = 'Kyle Covan — AI Builder, Strategist, and Partner';
const description =
  'Kyle Covan — AI Builder, Strategist, and Partner. Startup operations meets AI agent orchestration. ' +
  'Building a personal AI OS and an AI-powered second brain in public.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Person',
      '@id': 'https://kylecovan.com/#kyle',
      name: 'Kyle Covan',
      url: 'https://kylecovan.com/',
      image: 'https://kylecovan.com/og.png',
      jobTitle: 'AI Builder, Strategist, and Partner',
      email: 'mailto:kyle@kylecovan.com',
      description:
        "Kyle Covan builds AI agents and automations that take repetitive work off a person's plate. " +
        'Years in startup operations, now AI orchestration.',
      knowsAbout: ['AI agents', 'AI automation', 'Startup operations', 'Workflow automation'],
      sameAs: [
        'https://www.youtube.com/@KyleCovan',
        'https://x.com/kylecovan',
        'https://www.linkedin.com/in/kylecovan/',
      ],
    },
    {
      '@type': 'WebSite',
      '@id': 'https://kylecovan.com/#website',
      url: 'https://kylecovan.com/',
      name: 'Kyle Covan',
      description:
        'Startup operations meets AI agent orchestration. Building a personal AI OS and an ' +
        'AI-powered second brain in public.',
      inLanguage: 'en',
      publisher: { '@id': 'https://kylecovan.com/#kyle' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ProfilePage',
      '@id': 'https://kylecovan.com/#profilepage',
      url: 'https://kylecovan.com/',
      name: title,
      isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://kylecovan.com/#website' },
      about: { '@id': 'https://kylecovan.com/#kyle' },
      primaryImageOfPage: 'https://kylecovan.com/og.png',
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/"
  showWatching={true}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>

  <header class="masthead">
    <img class="portrait" src={portrait} width="156" height="156"
         alt="Kyle Covan" decoding="async">
    <div class="masthead-text">
      <h1>Kyle Covan</h1>
      <p class="creed">Striving to put Jesus Christ first</p>
      <p class="role">AI Builder, Strategist, and Partner</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section id="story" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Story</p>

    <h2 id="story-heading">Laying music down</h2>
    <p>
      For decades I poured my energy into music, but I realized music had
      become a stumbling block of pride, even though I was in denial about how
      much it pulled my focus away from what mattered most. Late in 2025 I was
      convicted of how big that stumbling block had become. By the grace of
      God the appetite for creating music left me entirely. What I had chased
      for decades, I now
      wanted taken away. So I gladly (and gratefully) laid music down. For me
      the benefit came immediately. I had more time, energy, and desire to put
      Jesus Christ first in my life.
    </p>
    <p>
      In the following nine months I wasn't sure what kind of long-term work I
      would do, or how I would carry the
      responsibilities Jesus Christ has given me: my wife, our bills, a
      household to provide for. Other changes were underway too. We had
      recently moved across the country. In God's timing, the desire and drive
      to learn and build AI surfaced.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today I build AI agents and automations that take repetitive work off a
      person's plate, and I aim to help others manage their businesses and
      lives more effectively. My prayer is that I approach this new work with
      reverence and an appropriate fear and trembling before God. Music showed
      me how quietly a good thing can take first place in my life, and I don't
      want AI to become the thing music was.
    </p>
    {/* Anna, in Kyle's exact words. Last on purpose: "every step of this
        journey" looks back over the whole section, so it only lands once all
        three paragraphs above have been read. Don't move it or reword it. */}
    <p>
      I am deeply grateful for my wife, Anna. She has been my constant
      partner, supporter, and helper since long before we even started dating,
      standing by me in every step of this journey.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>

    <h2 id="approach-heading">Startup operations, now AI orchestration</h2>
    <p>
      My years in startup operations gave me an understanding of how work
      actually moves through a business, and where it gets stuck. I look for
      the bottlenecks first, then automate only where it earns its place. Done
      well, a business gets more out of what it already has, and the people
      doing the work become managers of agents rather than the ones repeating
      the steps.
    </p>
    <p>
      Building and deploying a system is only half the work. A tool does no
      good unless people actually use it, so I care as much about hands-on
      training and steady check-ins as I do about the build itself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="building" aria-labelledby="building-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Building in public</p>

    <h2 id="building-heading">Two systems, built for myself first</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Documented as I go. These are personal projects, not packaged offers.
    </p>

    {projects.map(p => (
      <article class="project">
        <p class="project-index">{p.index}</p>
        <h3 class="project-title">{p.name} <span class="qualifier">{p.qualifier}</span></h3>
        <p class="one-liner">{p.oneLiner}</p>
        <p class="more"><a href={`/building/#${p.id}`}>Read the build log</a></p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>

    <h2 id="contact-heading">Reach out anytime</h2>

    <p>
      <a class="email" href="mailto:kyle@kylecovan.com">kyle@kylecovan.com</a>
    </p>

    {/* The line breaks inside these tags are load-bearing: each sits between a
        `>` and the next `<a`, so the separators keep their exact 0.35rem
        margins with no stray whitespace text node. Don't reflow this block. */}
    <p class="socials">
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@KyleCovan" rel="me">YouTube</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span
      ><a href="https://x.com/kylecovan" rel="me">X</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span
      ><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kylecovan/" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
    </p>

    <p class="closing">
      <a href="https://tapocanyon.com">Tapo Canyon</a> is where I work with
      clients.
      <span class="note">
        This page is personal. That one is for business.
      </span>
    </p>
  </section>

</Base>
